cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Tiny CyberLab (TCL): A reproducible Docker-based cyber range for project-based cybersecurity education"
message: "If you use this software or its lab materials, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Elhadad"
    given-names: "Saaid"
    affiliation: "Capital Community College"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"   # add if available
repository-code: "https://github.com/ielhadad/tiny-cyberlab"
abstract: >-
  Tiny CyberLab (TCL) is a small, reproducible cyber range that runs an entire
  attack-and-defend teaching environment as Docker containers on a single host.
  It provides 18 NICE-framework-aligned labs for project-based and experiential
  cybersecurity education, designed to lower the cost and complexity barriers to
  hands-on practice in higher education.
keywords:
  - cybersecurity education
  - cyber range
  - project-based learning
  - experiential learning
  - NICE framework
  - Docker
license: MIT
license-url: "https://github.com/ielhadad/tiny-cyberlab/blob/main/LICENSE"
version: "1.2.0"
date-released: "2026-10-02"

